    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>Acumenpopup is a lightweight and powerful popup builder that lets you create stunning popups directly inside the WordPress Block Editor (Gutenberg). Stop wrestling with complex settings panels—design your popups exactly like you write your posts.</p>\n<p><strong>🚀 Why Acumenpopup?</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Native Block Editor Experience:</strong> Build popups using the interface you already know.</li>\n<li><strong>Lightweight &amp; Fast:</strong> Optimized for performance with no bloat.</li>\n<li><strong>Conversion Focused:</strong> Built-in analytics to track views and conversions.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>✨ Key Features</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Visual Builder:</strong> Drag and drop blocks to create any layout.</li>\n<li><strong>Custom Blocks:</strong> Includes specialized blocks like Containers, Forms, Buttons, Icons, and Advanced Images.</li>\n<li><strong>Smart Triggers:</strong> Control when your popup appears (e.g., On Page Load).</li>\n<li><strong>Display Rules:</strong> Manage frequency with cookie-based retargeting (e.g., show once per session, or every X days).</li>\n<li><strong>Built-in Analytics:</strong> Track Impressions, Conversions, and Conversion Rates directly from the dashboard.</li>\n<li><strong>Mobile Responsive:</strong> Popups look great on all devices.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>🛠 Included Blocks</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Popup Builder:</strong> The main wrapper for your popup content.</li>\n<li><strong>Opt-in Form:</strong> Collect emails and leads easily.</li>\n<li><strong>Advanced Image:</strong> Flexible image controls.</li>\n<li><strong>Container:</strong> For layout and grouping.</li>\n<li><strong>Buttons &amp; Icons:</strong> For calls to action.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>External Services</h3>\n<p>This plugin connects to Google Fonts in order to load custom web fonts selected by the user inside the popup block editor.</p>\n<p><strong>What is it?</strong><br />\nGoogle Fonts is a free font-hosting service provided by Google LLC. It is used to render custom typography chosen for popup blocks.</p>\n<p><strong>What data is sent and when?</strong><br />\nWhen a visitor loads a page that contains a popup using a non-system font, the visitor&#8217;s browser sends a request to <code>fonts.googleapis.com</code> to download the selected font file. This request may include the visitor&#8217;s IP address and browser user-agent, as is standard with any external resource request. No personally identifiable data is collected or sent by this plugin beyond what a normal browser request includes.</p>\n<p><strong>Conditions:</strong><br />\nFont requests are only made when:<br />\n1. A popup campaign is active and published.<br />\n2. The popup uses a custom Google Font (i.e. a font other than system defaults like Arial, Georgia, Verdana, etc.).</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin files to the <code>/wp-content/plugins/acumen-popup</code> directory, or install the plugin through the WordPress plugins screen directly.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the &#8216;Plugins&#8217; screen in WordPress.</li>\n<li>Navigate to <strong>Campaigns</strong> in the admin menu to start creating your first popup.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id=\"does%20this%20modify%20my%20theme%20files%3F\">\nDoes this modify my theme files?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>No, Acumenpopup works independently and injects popups securely into your site footer.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id=\"can%20i%20use%20other%20gutenberg%20blocks%20inside%20the%20popup%3F\">\nCan I use other Gutenberg blocks inside the popup?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes! While we provide optimized blocks, you can use standard WordPress blocks within the popup container.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial release.</li>\n<li>Visual Popup Builder based on Gutenberg.</li>\n<li>Basic triggers and cookie control.</li>\n<li>Conversion tracking system.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Create high-converting popups and opt-in forms visually using the native WordPress Block Editor.",
    "description": "<p>Acumenpopup is a lightweight and powerful popup builder that lets you create stunning popups directly inside the WordPress Block Editor (Gutenberg). Stop wrestling with complex settings panels—design your popups exactly like you write your posts.</p>\n<p><strong>🚀 Why Acumenpopup?</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Native Block Editor Experience:</strong> Build popups using the interface you already know.</li>\n<li><strong>Lightweight &amp; Fast:</strong> Optimized for performance with no bloat.</li>\n<li><strong>Conversion Focused:</strong> Built-in analytics to track views and conversions.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>✨ Key Features</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Visual Builder:</strong> Drag and drop blocks to create any layout.</li>\n<li><strong>Custom Blocks:</strong> Includes specialized blocks like Containers, Forms, Buttons, Icons, and Advanced Images.</li>\n<li><strong>Smart Triggers:</strong> Control when your popup appears (e.g., On Page Load).</li>\n<li><strong>Display Rules:</strong> Manage frequency with cookie-based retargeting (e.g., show once per session, or every X days).</li>\n<li><strong>Built-in Analytics:</strong> Track Impressions, Conversions, and Conversion Rates directly from the dashboard.</li>\n<li><strong>Mobile Responsive:</strong> Popups look great on all devices.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>🛠 Included Blocks</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Popup Builder:</strong> The main wrapper for your popup content.</li>\n<li><strong>Opt-in Form:</strong> Collect emails and leads easily.</li>\n<li><strong>Advanced Image:</strong> Flexible image controls.</li>\n<li><strong>Container:</strong> For layout and grouping.</li>\n<li><strong>Buttons &amp; Icons:</strong> For calls to action.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>External Services</h3>\n<p>This plugin connects to Google Fonts in order to load custom web fonts selected by the user inside the popup block editor.</p>\n<p><strong>What is it?</strong><br />\nGoogle Fonts is a free font-hosting service provided by Google LLC. It is used to render custom typography chosen for popup blocks.</p>\n<p><strong>What data is sent and when?</strong><br />\nWhen a visitor loads a page that contains a popup using a non-system font, the visitor&#8217;s browser sends a request to <code>fonts.googleapis.com</code> to download the selected font file. This request may include the visitor&#8217;s IP address and browser user-agent, as is standard with any external resource request. No personally identifiable data is collected or sent by this plugin beyond what a normal browser request includes.</p>\n<p><strong>Conditions:</strong><br />\nFont requests are only made when:<br />\n1. A popup campaign is active and published.<br />\n2. The popup uses a custom Google Font (i.e. a font other than system defaults like Arial, Georgia, Verdana, etc.).</p>\n",
